  Lochs = ln(2)*ln(10) / zeta(2)
  The 6 comes from zeta(2)=pi^2/6, not directly from n=6
  But: zeta(2) = pi^2/6 and sigma_-1(6)=2 and pi^2/6 = sum 1/k^2
  zeta(2) = (2pi)^2 * |B_2| / (2*2!) where B_2 = 1/6
  B_2 = 1/6 = curiosity constant!
  >> Grade: 🟩  Error: 0.0000%    NOTE: 6 from zeta(2)=pi^2/6 via |B_2|=1/6=curiosity -- structural

